 "source_type": "instagram",
 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DeORIsIsiWW/",
 "title": "5 Ways to Increase Video Watch Time",
 "topic": "content creation",
 "summary": "Chris Chung outlines five structural techniques to retain viewers and increase watch time on videos. By framing information around results, alternatives, contradictions, and conditional requirements, creators can keep audiences engaged. The key lesson is to structure content in a way that continuously rehooks the viewer to learn what comes next.",
 "key_points": [
  "Show results first and then explain what you did, allowing viewers to learn with each step.",
  "Frame choices by stating it is not A or B, but actually C, so viewers stay to find out what C is.",
  "State a common belief and immediately contradict it so viewers stay to understand why.",
  "Rehook viewers mid-video by saying 'here's the better way' or 'here's the best way' to maintain attention.",
  "Create urgency by stating 'this won't work unless you do this' so viewers stay to learn how."
 ],
 "content": "Post text: Video by iamchrischung. Make a note of this post.\n\nTranscript: 5 ways to make people watch longer. If you show the results first, then what you did, they will learn with each step. If you say it's not A or B, but it's actually C, they will stay for C. If you state a common belief and then contradict it, they will stay to hear why. If you say but here's the better way or but here's the best way, you will rehook them and they will keep watching. If you say but this won't work unless you do this, they will stay to hear how.\n\nText on screen:\n- 5 ways to make people watch longer (+107k followers)\n- Results First | What You Did | Learn | Step\n- A | B | C | Stay\n- Common Belief | Contradict | Stay | Why\n- Better Way | Best Way | Rehook | Watching\n- Won't Work | Unless | Stay | How",
